From: rdp-release-kit
Subject: [PATCH] libssl: always send psk_key_exchange_modes in a TLS 1.3 ClientHello

LibreSSL's TLS 1.3 client sends the psk_key_exchange_modes extension only
when it means to resume a session (use_psk_dhe_ke), so a first connection
carries none. Windows' own TLS stack (Schannel) then fails while issuing its
NewSessionTicket and ends the connection with an internal_error alert: with
RDP, right after the handshake, on the first CredSSP message. OpenSSL always
sends the extension (psk_dhe_ke), and its clients connect.

Found and tested by freerdp-59 (a minimal LibreSSL client against Windows 11:
0/3 with the alert, 3/3 with this). LibreSSL 4.4.0, ssl/ssl_tlsext.c.
---
--- a/ssl/ssl_tlsext.c	2026-10-22 03:56:43.904038046 -0400
+++ b/ssl/ssl_tlsext.c	2026-10-31 05:13:09.508000000 -0400
@@ -1996,8 +1996,9 @@
 static int
 tlsext_psk_kex_modes_client_needs(SSL *s, uint16_t msg_type)
 {
-	return (s->s3->hs.tls13.use_psk_dhe_ke &&
-	    s->s3->hs.our_max_tls_version >= TLS1_3_VERSION);
+	/* always offered, as OpenSSL does: Windows' Schannel aborts NLA over TLS 1.3
+	 * (internal_error while it issues the session ticket) without it */
+	return (s->s3->hs.our_max_tls_version >= TLS1_3_VERSION);
 }
 
 static int
